ing gain <img src=\"/media/13e49cd8454d6379ef89a43655c165844cd9ca80.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n</div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> <p>\n <img src=\"/media/3bc1fed55369e3d2d34eeecd14f7636b58f40d69.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n</div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> There are 3 forward path in SFG of given transfer function.</div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>\n (a, b, c)</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/a41fa7bcec9565253c701a0809400515c25cfcc7.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/a1b83aacb44c6d78f08caef84f5f87b7f868f155.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":24,"type":"NAT","correct":"","right":1,"wrong":0.33,"qtext":"<p>\n Consider the block diagram given shown in figure:</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/94cd5afa7c5f9cecbb00711f8390ae00a1709787.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p>\n The minimum value of <em>K</em> such that the steady state error for unit ramp input should not exceed by 1.25% is _____.</p></div>\n<div><span>NAT</span>","options":[],"nat":{"low":"127","high":"129"},"solution":"<p>\n 128 (127 - 129)</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/7ed1c4370e2ae7650be7a621991f0411cd56459b.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":25,"type":"MSQ","correct":"A,C,D","right":2,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>\n A unity feedback closed loop control system has <img src=\"/media/89ed26c4f3658301d24ea164d9eaabe8cc8660aa.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /> Which of the following statement(s) is/are correct about the system?</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> <p>\n The system is stable for <em>K</em> > –4</p>\n</div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> Phase cross-over frequency = 0</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> For K = 4, gain cross-over frequency = 0</div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> For K = 4, phase margin = 180°</div>","isCorrect":true}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>\n (a, c, d)</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/330b93adf836d5f1df151ac4daa29ef33f793ebc.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":26,"type":"NAT","correct":"","right":1,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>\n The root locus of the system with loop transfer function given below :</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/17f96c1288e9dded6c207ef5960e62e11c4c30ba.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p>\n Crosses the jω-axis at <em>K</em> = ________. (rounded off to two decimal places)</p></div>\n<div><span>NAT</span>","options":[],"nat":{"low":"1.5","high":"1.6"},"solution":"<p>\n 1.55 (1.50 - 1.60)</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/c87be32eefad3e4373399915f00fe0e4d5b31935.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/a30a3cf229ec76654e4e01e5a1ec49928d0d4a25.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":27,"type":"MSQ","correct":"B,C","right":2,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>\n The response of a system is <em>c</em>(<em>t</em>) = 1 + 0.2e<sup>–60t</sup> – 1.2<em>e<sup>–10t</sup></em> when subject to a unit step input. Which of the following statements is/are correct about the system?</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> The undamped natural frequency is 60 rad/sec.</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> The damping ratio is 1.43.</div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> <p>\n The closed loop transfer function of the system is <em>T</em>(<em>s</em>) = <img src=\"/media/805c8722e7b1dc1631973dce671f7234d7b6bf54.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n</div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> The settling time for 5% error is 0.114 sec.</div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>\n (b, c)</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/4ff7eec488b076ebd4abc2dedda704612a862641.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/656ad4db0e688d1485b680361dddc424517434c8.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":28,"type":"MCQ","correct":"B","right":2,"wrong":0.66,"qtext":"<p>\n Given the system represented in state space by equations:</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/0be7c8c915430ef35ca20f0c24a127aa93ae8458.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p>\n The state-transition matrix of the system is</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> <p>\n <img src=\"/media/2640d71b1ea146c30ad444d569967a13268afb47.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> <p>\n <img src=\"/media/5aafd684f0f08d7d25ced3823a96b0a1063230b2.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> <p>\n <img src=\"/media/469ed38c14dd7c67e77a850f0681e64735565f7e.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> <p>\n <img src=\"/media/a5fb6ce567684139d4c1231ac28f6ab1163fece9.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>\n (b)</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/88c8569a07c03f89442467ef725c1d4caea61a89.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/5217657ad0a696707cbcc351263813fed5bbef76.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":29,"type":"MCQ","correct":"C","right":2,"wrong":0.66,"qtext":"<p>\n A control system is designed to keep the antenna of tracking radar pointed at a flying target. The system must be able to follow a target travelling in straight line with speed of 250 m/sec with maximum permissible error of 0.01 degree. The shortest distance from antenna to target is 300 m. Find the value of error constant <img src=\"/media/e17ea26dd805a5eb8c8e3399f2528db456029479.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /> in order to satisfy the requirements is</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> 1.989</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> 7.956</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> 3.978</div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> 6.828</div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>\n (c)</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/bee9734142680be271a7c2b9e88917847d9af92c.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":30,"type":"MCQ","correct":"A","right":2,"wrong":0.66,"qtext":"<p>\n A first order system described by 1.5 <img src=\"/media/dccac2785fbf37d468582e539a5a0caa12a559de.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /> is subjected to sinusoidal input y(t) = 3 sin(ω<sub>0</sub>)<em>t </em>mV. Assume that the output of the system, goes into the filter that cut offs all input signal smaller in amplitude than 0.01 mV, the critical frequency ωe such that for all ω<sub>0</sub> > ω<sub>e</sub> the filter will not observe the input signal is</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> 200</div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> 400</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> 100</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> 50</div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>\n (a)</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/a176d2032c0c854d480fd378f5cd586ed754a891.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/a3f2ed2a682fc9d34cbd82f4fda77c55ee0298b8.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":31,"type":"MCQ","correct":"D","right":2,"wrong":0.66,"qtext":"<p>\n The largest time constant of the characteristics equation given below is ______ seconds.</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/1f521e1da9db38b4dad38a87e2a0cd3801cea835.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> 2 sec</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> 1.33 sec</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> 0.5 sec</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> 1 sec</div>","isCorrect":true}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>\n (d)</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/2bc4b395053c13650a27a8e93d8cc55e8b7faf02.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p>\n </p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":32,"type":"NAT","correct":"","right":2,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>\n The open-loop transfer function of a feedback system is <em>G</em>(<em>s</em>)<em>H</em>(<em>s</em>) = <img src=\"/media/29090c577fbd4ad88333396308a0c0a08ba8b348.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /> For <em>K</em> < 1, no. of closed loop poles lying R.H.S. of s-plane is</p></div>\n<div><span>NAT</span>","options":[],"nat":{"low":"1","high":"1"},"solution":"<p>\n 1 (1 - 1)</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/99bad54f4d57405ae082921369401cd54090c110.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":33,"type":"NAT","correct":"","right":2,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>\n The open-loop transfer function of a unity of feedback system is given by <img src=\"/media/8f3d42e961833038262719a1a16ad5fe21d77d1d.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /> Where A and B are positive constants. For reducing the peak overshoot of unit step response of system from 80% to 30%, the factor by which amplifier gain ‘A’ has to be reduced will be _____.<br />\n (Answer upto 3 decimal place)</p></div>\n<div><span>NAT</span>","options":[],"nat":{"low":"0.03","high":"0.045"},"solution":"<p>\n 0.0384 (0.030 - 0.045)</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/d61fee350aaec961eb7ad0235c94410fdf572768.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/bf7d183c8faee162d4cea3d5216f45a8a55dd38a.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"}],"questionCount":33,"parsedAt":"2026-11-10T19:39:11.173Z"}